SOAPBOX: The bands were open but signal levels were certainly well down.
SOAPBOX: At almost 62 I don't have the stamina for a full 36hrs of
SOAPBOX: operation anymore, rather to operate in stints and enjoy working
SOAPBOX: a pile-up or some juicy/rarish DX or give someone a needed mult.
SOAPBOX: Conditions to the USA were certainly down, with the usual big
SOAPBOX: guns well down on normal signal levels. The number of operators
SOAPBOX: from S.E. Asia especially YB continue to increase and without
SOAPBOX: many QSOs with BY, DU, 9M and YB my score would have been way
SOAPBOX: lower. Gone are the days were I could work 1500 to 2000 QSOs from
SOAPBOX: a modest but capable station in suburban VK. Definitely had fun
SOAPBOX: this time though, with some nice runs on 20m LP to EU. I miss
SOAPBOX: having good propagation to the USA where there is no language
SOAPBOX: barrier (except my darn aussie accent) and the operators are
SOAPBOX: skilled and quick. Thanks for another good show. I am also a
SOAPBOX: tri-bander single element class station.
